  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Carved Monoliths at the Ancient (1600 BC) Archaeological Site of Cerro Sechin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The pre-Incan site of Cerro Sechin is well known for the approximately 300 carved stone bas-reliefs of warrior priests and other figures decorating one of the site&apos;s surviving buildings. This project includes the conservation of reliefs most at risk.</narrative>
  </description>
